"Sophia.8hearts.22": "!!!$0",
"Sophia.8hearts.23": "You're so cute!",
"Sophia.8hearts.24": "Hey, you!$1#$b#I'm in the middle of reading a graphic novel!$9",
"Sophia.8hearts.25": "Um...$1#$b#I'm getting out of the house more. I think spending time with other people helps me.$1",
"Sophia.8hearts.26": "...$0",
"Sophia.8hearts.27": "I'm still scared you know.$2#$b#My thoughts still drift, to those moments and it feels like I'm back to how I've always been.$2",
"Sophia.8hearts.28": "I've finally understood the core of my problem but that doesn't mean that it just magically dissapears.$0#$b#Although bad memories are part of what define me, I can't let them dictate my life like they did for so long.$0#$b#But it's hard to control them, one slip and you fall down and endless pit that you can't get out of.$2",
"Sophia.8hearts.29": "I can't do much about it but for now, I'm trying to improve little by little everyday.$1#$b#I've been talking with Dr. Harvey to help me find a therapist.$0#$b#I'll probably have my appointments online so I don't have to travel to Zuzu City everytime.$0#$b#I've also been wanting to try doing something new in the vineyard that isn't the same old Blue Moon Wine.$1",
"Sophia.8hearts.30": "I've been so convinced that my whole life would be the same that I thought it was stupid to think I could improve.$6#$b#But now that I'm putting an effort, I can see a sliver of hope.$1#$b#Hope that I can surpass this.$1#$b#For the first time of my life, it finally feels like I'm on the right path.$9#$b#As long as I can believe that I can one day I can do it then maybe, just maybe I might actualy be able to achieve it.$9",
"Sophia.8hearts.31": "I never quite understood why you put up with everything.$0#$b#Not everyone is willing to listen through other people's problems or even help clean their parent's room.$0#$b#But I'm grateful to you for being supportive through all of this, for being such a great friend.$9",
"Sophia.8hearts.32": "Do you have some time? Come over here, I want to show you this page.$1#$b#You'll get a laugh out of it!$9",
"Sophia.8hearts.33": "Sophia showed me funny pictures in her book. We laughed and talked about her day.",
"Sophia.8hearts.34": "I'm in a really good mood today!$1#$b#How are you?$9#$e#OoOoh! I see!$1#$e#Hey, talk to you some other time?$9#$e#%Sophia smiles at you.",
//22



    //9th Event Sophia Date(?) in Vineyard
"Sophia.12hearts2.01": "You're here!$1#$b#Um. We can start harvesting this field first.$0#$b#Let's grab our garden snips and baskets!$9",
"Sophia.12hearts2.02": "Hey!$1",
"Sophia.12hearts2.03": "You look cute over there...$4",
"Sophia.12hearts2.04": "We're finally done! Free at last!$9",
"Sophia.12hearts2.05": "Hey. There's something I want to share with you...$0",
"Sophia.12hearts2.06": "Um...$2",
"Sophia.12hearts2.07": "I want to share my family's secret grape fermentation method with you...$1#$b#It's what makes Blue Moon Vineyard's wine taste so special...$1",
"Sophia.12hearts2.08": "I received Sophia's vineyard trade secrets! She really trusted me with this! Grapes are now worth twice as much.",
"Sophia.12hearts2.09": "*giggles*$9#$b#It's a family secret, and we're family now.$4",
"Sophia.12hearts2.10": "We should have more adventures like this. Something... different.$4#$b#Now how about we sit down and watch something on TV? We could watch anime or umm something else if you'd like.$1",
"Sophia.12hearts2.11": "Let's see here. Where did I put Season 1 of 'Sailor Sun'?$1",
"Sophia.12hearts2.12": "Huh? What's this?$0",
"Sophia.12hearts2.13": "Sophia is holding a dusty VHS tape in her hand",
"Sophia.12hearts2.14": "I forgot we had VHS tapes here, the only ones who used them were...$0",
"Sophia.12hearts2.15": "I-I need to watch this. Could you take a seat over there? I'll figure out how to use it...$0",
"Sophia.12hearts2.16": "There, it should work now.$0",
"Sophia.12hearts2.17": "The figure a woman and a kid sitting on a picnic blanket over a green field can be seen, the camera is being held shakily by someone",
"Sophia.12hearts2.18": "Man's voice: Smile at the camera Alice, I want your pretty face preserved for ages to come.",
"Sophia.12hearts2.19": "Alice: Come on Bob, you don't need a camera, you already get to see my face every single day don't you? Now come over and eat your food, I got all your favourites.",
"Sophia.12hearts2.20": "Kid: Yeah! Come over or I'll eat all of your food instead.",
"Sophia.12hearts2.21": "Alice: What a voracious little kid, I wonder who they got it from.",
"Sophia.12hearts2.22": "Bob: Hahaha! You both make a compelling argument. Now how do I turn this off?",
"Sophia.12hearts2.23": "...$2",
"Sophia.12hearts2.24": "It still feels odd @.$0#$b#I should be feeling happy to find something like this, a sweet memory from my parent's that they left behind.$2#$b#But all I can feel is a bitter taste in my mouth.$2",
"Sophia.12hearts2.25": "I need some time alone to think about this. About these feelings I have.$2#$b#Sadness is an important aspect to our lives but just how much should I let it be part of me?$0#$b#You can head on home @, I think I'll stay here for a while...$0",
"Sophia.12hearts2.26": "I took some time to think. I still don't have any definitive answers but it feels like I'm getting closer to an answer.$1#$b#What did you think of my parents? I don't think you've ever seen them. They would have loved you.$1",


  
    //8th(?) Sophia Rose Event
"Sophia.RoseEvent.01": "Oh. Hey @ it's nice to see you.$9",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.02": "Come here, I want to show you the thing I talked about in the mail.$1",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.03": "This is something I've been working on, it's called Rosé wine.$1",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.04": "Sophia opens the tap on the keg and a pink liquid pours out.",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.05": "Normally for red wines you leave the grape skin to ferment alongside the wine.$1#$b#But in this case I only leave the skin for a few hours so it only absorbs a bit of the skin's hue and flavour.$1#$b#I made it with the grapes you provided so I think you deserve to get the first drink.$9#$b#It's very different from the wines I usually make.$0",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.06": "I've never had the chance to do something like this.$2#$b#Blue Moon Wine, just like any other wine, has it's distinct taste, an image that needs to be maintained.$0#$b#Ever since I took to managing the vineyard I've had to uphold that image.$0#$b#But no matter how hard I tried, I could never truly replicate the wine my parents made.$2#$b#Something was always off and I could never find the solution.$2#$b#But now...$0",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.07": "I don't feel like I need to recklesly try to imitate it anymore.$1#$b#I will never be able to recreate their wine and that's okay.$1#$b#Blue Moon Wine doesn't have to be the same forever, things can change.$9#$b#And I hope that this wine can be the first step towards something new.$1",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.08": "Now how about we go try it! The first glass is yours remember?$9",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.09": "Me and Sophia tasted her new wine. It has a dry taste like Blue Moon Wines but with a strong floral flavour that made it stand out on its own.",
"Sophia.RoseEvent.10": "That tasted better than I thought!$9#$b#Here, have a bottle for the road. If you want more you can get some from the ledger.[degradingwindow.SophiaRewritten_Rose_Wine]$1",



    //Kid Having?th Sophia Final Event
"Sophia.FinalEvent.01": "Hey you! It took a while but I finally got %kid1 to take a little nap.$9#$b#They're growing up so fast, I never imagined myself becoming a parent and building a family.$1#$b#Ever since I lost mine it almost felt like I was doomed to live alone. But meeting you changed that.$1#$b#...$2",
"Sophia.FinalEvent.02": "I've been thinking about the future a lot... about... our death...$2#$b#When we die, will %kid1 fall into the same pit that I did?$2#$b#Will they live a whole life of sadness with the knowledge of our deaths gnawing away at them every single day?$2",
"Sophia.FinalEvent.03": "These happy days we've had with %kid1 have been so precious to me.$1#$b#But when we die.... it would almost be like they never existed at all.$2#$b#It's unfair that the legacy of our entire life is decided by one single moment, a fragment of what we are...$2#$b#That the most defining memory we leave behind is tragic one and that our loved ones suffer because of us...$2",
"Sophia.FinalEvent.04": "But I've realized it doesn't have to be that way anymore.$1#$b#I don't want to remember my parent's for just their deaths, and I'm sure they wouldn't want that either.$1#$b#Our lives are so much more than just that one single moment.$9#$b#Death is sad, tragic and horrible but compared to the rest of our life, it's only a glimpse of what defines us.$1",
"Sophia.FinalEvent.05": "I want %kid1 to know that. I want them to look back at us not with sadness but with a smile on their face.$9#$b#Promise me we'll give %kid1 the best memories that a parent can give their child.$8",

